Walk a directory and extract metadata for every file.

Per-file failures are reported but do not abort the run. If any
file fails, the command exits 2 after printing the full report
(per docs/recon.md §8).

By default only the immediate children of <dir> are processed; use
--recursive to descend into sub-directories.

Usage:
  usulnet meta scan <dir> [flags]

Examples:
  usulnet meta scan ./photos
  usulnet meta scan ./photos --recursive
  usulnet meta scan ./photos --recursive --output json

Flags:
  -h, --help        help for scan
  -r, --recursive   recurse into subdirectories

Global Flags:
  -c, --config string    config file path (default: /etc/usulnet/config.yaml or ./config.yaml)
      --image string     toolkit image (local mode only; default $USULNET_RECON_TOOLKIT_IMAGE)
      --json             shortcut for --output json (overrides --output)
      --output string    output format: table|json|yaml (default "table")
  -q, --quiet            suppress informational output (errors and primary data still print)
      --server string    usulnet API URL (forces server mode; default $USULNET_API_URL)
      --timeout string   container timeout (e.g. 30s)
      --token string     API token (default $USULNET_API_TOKEN)
